{"term":"bombard","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:86eac83fd5d955600e","definition":"A medieval primitive cannon, used chiefly in sieges for throwing heavy stone balls.","example":"They planted in divers places twelve great bombards, wherewith they threw huge stones into the air, which, falling down into the city, might break down the houses.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a398c67703f384cf80","definition":"A bassoon-like medieval musical instrument.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:718a0f21e3ed3a1491","definition":"A large liquor container made of leather, in the form of a jug or a bottle.","example":"[…] yond same black cloud, yond huge one, / looks like a foul bombard that would shed his liquor.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7e27ff4945713cd9b3","definition":"A bombardment.","example":"With mines and parallels contracts the space;\nThen bids the battering floats his labors crown\nAnd pour their bombard on the shuddering town","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"poetic, rare","register":"poetic, rare","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bbc5c5b4680734e5a2","definition":"A bombardon.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:90e60a763af6ec2b5e","definition":"To continuously attack something with bombs, artillery shells or other missiles or projectiles.","example":"The enemy's stronghold was bombarded for 3 hours straight.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bomb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase","bombardable","bombardier","bombardment","microbombarded","unbombarded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:525f5c80ca67d44145","definition":"To attack something or someone by directing objects at them.","example":"My correspondent, who was riding in the first coach, comments that the small standard tender did not take kindly to this gay progress, and signified its disapproval from time to time by bombarding the train with lumps of coal!","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bomb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase","bombardable","bombardier","bombardment","microbombarded","unbombarded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ce630246a644784c0e","definition":"To continuously send or direct (at someone)","example":"I was bombarded with WhatsApp messages after appearing on the news.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bomb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase","bombardable","bombardier","bombardment","microbombarded","unbombarded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:41bebff38ae475c84d","definition":"To direct at a substance an intense stream of high-energy particles, usually sub-atomic or made of at most a few atoms.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bomb"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase","bombardable","bombardier","bombardment","microbombarded","unbombarded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6254a09746aab420d4","definition":"A surname from French.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase","bombardable","bombardier","bombardment","microbombarded","unbombarded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bombard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈbɒmˌbɑːd/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/78/En-us-bombard.ogg/En-us-bombard.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["bombardman","bombard phrase","bombardable","bombardier","bombardment","microbombarded","unbombarded"]}